{"kind":"request","text":"Planner decision 40ea8fdf, route 1 of aaf573dd. found and first-key do not refuse a founder key that is also the recovery key. A stolen key in that shape keeps the recovery key's authority after its revocation: the recovery-key grant passes invite-member, invite-key, remove-member, revoke-key and rotate-recovery, and each accepted act restarts its signed read of membership. The command line and the page always make a separate key, so only a hand-built found reaches this shape. Owner: builder.","body":{"conditions":"A found or first-key whose founder key equals the recovery key is refused, and a new room keeps the two keys apart at creation as join and enrol do. Existing rooms are not repaired. Done when a scope test holds the refusal at each act, a control shows each, the review request names any new Membership or Directory definition pin, and the gate passes.","target_head":"8ae17cb229d22b08f4e7e48b9a46e12ab16fbc64","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}